> **ARCHIVE — Debrief redaction page (in-world)**
>
> **SUBJ: F2F EXCHANGE — RETURN TEAM 1965/78**
>
> Transfer ID **F2F-1965-0412** … duration **4680** … [REDACTED] … public release **DENIED** …
>
> *(Page **Invented**; fields rhyme McKinnon spreadsheet row.)*

---

In 2001 a man in Crouch End whispered **Non-Terrestrial Officers** at a screen.

In 1978 a captain whispered nothing at a debrief table and carried two suns behind his eyes into a country that wanted him to be normal again.

Normal was a password field that was not empty.

Normal was a life without integers.

Normal was not offered.

The return was complete.

The story was not.

Compartmentalisation was a kind of violence done to memory.

Violence done to memory eventually leaked.

That was the hope Gary would live on without knowing its name.

That was the hope **Anonymous** would exploit in 2005 on a forum Gary would read in 2006 with cold tea and a printout under a bed.

Fleet to fleet.

Return pending.

Leak pending.

Truth pending in the only sense truth ever arrives for people without security clearance: badly indexed, poorly secured, reachable from a flat in North London if you are rude enough to try an empty password.

The debrief ended.

The vault closed.

The integer remained.

**4680.**

Thirteen years.

Non-terrestrial officers.

The believing register held because the forms compiled.

The forms always compile.

That is why Gary believed them.

That is why the reader believes this chapter, and why ch-99 will audit it without mercy.
